{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return rule","requirement":"A landlord may not require a security deposit above one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% interest per year, and return it with an itemized list of damages within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 5% interest per year; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Any residential tenancy in which the lessor accepts a security deposit; the section states no building age, unit count or owner limits.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Liability on transfer does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60 or a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution. No deduction is allowed for damage listed in the condition statement.","penalty":"Tenant awarded three times the security deposit or balance due, plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees; landlord forfeits the right to retain any deposit for failure to deposit funds, itemize damages, transfer the deposit or return it.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2)","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on advance payments before tenancy","requirement":"At or before a tenancy begins, a landlord or agent may require only first month's rent, last month's rent, a security deposit equal to one month's rent, and the cost of a key and lock, and may not demand other upfront amounts.","key_value":"First month's rent + last month's rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key and lock cost; fee in lieu of deposit capped at 1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Applies at or prior to the commencement of any residential tenancy; the fee-in-lieu-of-deposit rules apply only where the lessor offers such a fee.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"The optional fee in lieu of a security deposit applies only where the lessor offers it; the fee is optional for both tenant and lessor and the tenant may pay the deposit instead.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following: (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy; and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit offer and credit/income neutrality rule","requirement":"A landlord offering a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every approved applicant regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, household size or credit score, and may not use those factors to set the fee.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"A lessor who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit; the rule governs how that option is offered and how the fee amount is set.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies to a lessor who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit to an applicant whose application for occupancy has been approved.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score; and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
